<title>HUNGARY: Hungary MKB bank 96 pre-tax profit up at HUF9.2bln.</title>
<headline>Hungary MKB bank 96 pre-tax profit up at HUF9.2bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending on December 31,</p>
<p>1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>						1996		 1995</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			9,217	 vs   6,101</p>
<p>    Taxation				1,655	 vs   1,206</p>
<p>    After-tax profit		    7,562	 vs   4,895</p>
<p>Result on financial</p>
<p>	 activities			 9,854	 vs   6,665</p>
<p>    Net interest income		13,368	 vs  11,386</p>
<p>    Dividends, profit received	  386	 vs     252</p>
<p>Income from other financial</p>
<p>	 activities			11,186	 vs   7,896</p>
<p>    Other income			  5,244	 vs   5,893</p>
<p>Expenditures on other fin.</p>
<p>	 activities			 6,883	 vs   4,216</p>
<p>    Other expenditures		  7,275	 vs   9,482</p>
<p>    Operating costs		     6,172	 vs   5,064</p>
<p>Result on non-fin. activities</p>
<p>	 and extraord. result	     637 loss  vs     564 loss</p>
<p>NOTE: The figures are unconsolidated and based on the Hungarian Accounting Standard. Magyar Kulkereskedelmi Bank Rt (MKB) is 58.2 percent owned by Germany's Bayerische Landesbank Girozentrale. The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) holds 16.7 percent of MKB's shares, while Deutsche Investitions und Entwicklungs gmbH owns 8.3 percent. MKB itself holds some 6.5 percent of its shares.</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
